/-!
# The eta powers `h₃ = η⁸` and `h₄ = η⁶` (Proposition 4.5(a))

For `N ∈ {3, 4}` let `k_N = 12 / N` and `h_N = η^{2 k_N} = η^{24 / N}`. We show that `h_N` is a
modular form of weight `k_N` on `Γ(N)`, that `h_N ^ N = Δ`, and that its `q`-expansion in
`q^{1/N}` (`UpperHalfPlane.qExpansion N`) is the integral power series
`X ∏_{n ≥ 1} (1 - X^{N n})^{24 / N}`.

## Proof of slash invariance (manuscript, Proposition 4.5(a))

For `γ ∈ SL(2, ℤ)` the function `g = h_N ∣[k_N] γ` satisfies `g ^ N = Δ ∣[12] γ = Δ = h_N ^ N`, so
`g / h_N` is a continuous function on the connected space `ℍ` with values in the finite set `μ_N`,
hence a constant `ζ`: `h_N ∣[k_N] γ = ζ • h_N`. Since `h_N(τ) = q^{1/N} ∏ (1 - qⁿ)^{24/N}` is
periodic of period `N`, `h_N ∣[k_N] (γ T^N γ⁻¹) = h_N`. The stabilizer of `h_N` under the slash
action is a subgroup, so it contains the normal closure of `T^N`, which contains `Γ(N)`
(`CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma_le_normalClosure_T_pow`; this algebraic statement replaces the
manuscript's covering-space argument that `Γ(N)` is generated by parabolic elements).
Boundedness at all cusps follows from `h_N ∣[k_N] γ = ζ • h_N` and `h_N → 0` at `i∞`.

## The `q`-expansion

The partial products `P_M = X (∏_{n < M} (1 - X^{N(n+1)}))^{24/N} ∈ ℤ[X]` converge locally
uniformly on the unit disc to the function `F(q) = q ∏_{n ≥ 1} (1 - q^{N n})^{24/N}`, which agrees
with the cusp function of `h_N`. Hence the Taylor coefficients of `F` at `0` (the `q`-expansion
coefficients of `h_N`) are the limits of those of `P_M`, which stabilize.

## Main results

* `EtaPower.etaPowerForm N hN : ModularForm (Gamma N) (12 / N : ℕ)`, with values
  `η(τ) ^ (24 / N)` (`EtaPower.etaPowerForm_apply`); `EtaPower.etaPowerThree`,
  `EtaPower.etaPowerFour` for `N = 3, 4`.
* `EtaPower.etaPowerForm_pow_apply`: `h_N(τ) ^ N = Δ(τ)`.
* `EtaPower.qExpansion_etaPowerForm`: `qExpansion N h_N` is the image of `EtaPower.qSeries N`.
* `EtaPower.exists_integral_qExpansion`.
-/

public section

